  },
  "interaction_pairing": {
    "user_action": "User asked: 'why are you searching or matching too senior roles? The AG brain should exactly know the skill set, the experience level and the profile details and then only the match should be done.' Also: 'ensure that the job experience is selected according to profile since it is a fresher with internship.'",
    "ai_response_quality": "High — identified two root causes: (1) match_threshold=40 allowed 40% LLM score matches through, (2) hardcoded `cand_exp + 3` accepted roles requiring up to 3.5 yrs. Fixed both. match_threshold raised to 65. max_experience_gap_years=2 added to config. Python code now reads gap dynamically from config.",
    "friction_points": "Initial analysis focused only on the LLM scoring. Had to additionally recognize that the Stage 1 hard gate (experience band) was also miscalibrated.",
    "resolution": "candidate_config.json: match_threshold 40→65, max_experience_gap_years:2 added. core/ai_client.py evaluate_job_match(): cand_exp+3 → cand_exp+_max_gap (from config). Net effect: roles requiring >2.5 yrs hard-rejected at Stage 1. LLM must score ≥65% to pass (previously 40%)."
